From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:26:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] net: stmmac: count the whole page as the truesize of an
 RX fragment

Each RX buffer is a page pool page of napi_skb_frag_size bytes, but
skb_add_rx_frag() was given dma_buf_sz. With 2032-byte buffers on 4 KiB
pages, a socket was charged half the memory its frames hold.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
index 929ee69..081d61a 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
@@ -6072,7 +6072,7 @@ read_again:
 						buf1_len, dma_dir);
 			skb_add_rx_frag(skb, skb_shinfo(skb)->nr_frags,
 					buf->page, buf->page_offset, buf1_len,
-					priv->dma_conf.dma_buf_sz);
+					rx_q->napi_skb_frag_size);
 			buf->page = NULL;
 		}
 
@@ -6081,7 +6081,7 @@ read_again:
 						buf2_len, dma_dir);
 			skb_add_rx_frag(skb, skb_shinfo(skb)->nr_frags,
 					buf->sec_page, 0, buf2_len,
-					priv->dma_conf.dma_buf_sz);
+					rx_q->napi_skb_frag_size);
 			buf->sec_page = NULL;
 		}
 
